---
import ServiceLayout from 'theme/layouts/ServiceLayout.astro';

const serviceData = {
  title: 'Furniture Removals, Dismantling & Reassembly',
  slug: 'furniture-removals',
  metaTitle: 'Furniture Removals & Assembly London | Pearl Removals',
  metaDescription: 'Specialist furniture removals, dismantling & reassembly in North West London. Flat-pack, antique wardrobes, modular sofas & designer tables rebuilt expertly.',
  heroHeading: 'Furniture Removals, Dismantling & Assembly in London',
  heroSubheading: 'Careful disassembly, secure transit, and exact reassembly of modular wardrobes, designer beds, dining suites, and fragile office furniture.',
  icon: 'tool',
  summary: 'Professional furniture handling with full toolkits, hardware sorting, and structural assembly for modern flat-pack and oversized heritage pieces.',
  priceFrom: 95,
  priceUnit: 'item',
  priceNotes: 'Competitive rates per item or integrated into a comprehensive home move. Fully insured disassembly and reassembly with all fixings catalogued.',
  benefits: [
    'Fully equipped toolkits including metric/imperial allen keys, cordless impact drivers, and torque bits',
    'Hardware bag tagging ensuring every bolt, dowel, cam lock, and bracket is preserved with its host furniture',
    'Experience with high-end designer brands (Poliform, Ligne Roset, BoConcept) as well as complex IKEA PAX systems',
    'Heavy-duty quilted furniture covers, corner edge bumpers, and stretch shrink wraps for safe stair handling',
    'Wall-fixing anchoring services for tall bookcases and children\'s wardrobe safety in your new residence',
    'Full £50,000 Goods in Transit insurance protecting furniture components against transit wear'
  ],
  whatsIncluded: [
    'Systematic disassembly of multi-door wardrobes, ottoman beds, bunk beds, and extending dining tables',
    'Detailed labelling and photographic recording of complex cable runs or internal mechanisms',
    'Dedicated padded wrapping of loose panels, glass shelves, and mirrored wardrobe sliding doors',
    'Hardware pouching attached directly to the primary structural frame of each item',
    'Level alignment and door hinge calibration during reassembly at your destination property',
    'Removal of all protective wrapping, tape, and packaging materials post-installation'
  ],
  whatsNotIncluded: [
    'Structural wall reinforcement into crumbling lath-and-plaster without specialist masonry plugs',
    'Reassembly of structural furniture items where original factory chipboard dowel holes have stripped',
    'Plumbing, gas connection, or hardwired electrical wiring inside integrated furniture units'
  ],
  process: [
    {
      step: 1,
      title: 'Survey & Disassembly Strategy',
      description: 'We evaluate which items require dismantling to pass through tight hallways, measuring door frame clearances and recording complex hinge or drawer slide mechanics.'
    },
    {
      step: 2,
      title: 'Precision Disassembly & Hardware Tagging',
      description: 'Using professional tools, we take down frames without straining joints. All screws, brackets, and cams are bagged, labelled, and taped to their matching structural parts.'
    },
    {
      step: 3,
      title: 'Padded Transit & Vehicle Stowing',
      description: 'Disassembled panels, slats, and glass components are wrapped in thick transit blankets and strapped flat against load-bearing vehicle walls.'
    },
    {
      step: 4,
      title: 'Destination Reassembly & Hinge Alignment',
      description: 'In your chosen room, we rebuild the furniture to manufacturer tolerances, plumb wardrobe doors, level legs on uneven floors, and verify stability.'
    }
  ],
  premiumAngle: 'For luxury properties in Hampstead, St John\'s Wood, and Belsize Park with bespoke joinery, Italian modular wardrobes, and marble tabletops, our master assembly technicians provide millimeter-precise levelling and pristine white-glove finish.',
  faqs: [
    {
      question: 'Can you dismantle and rebuild large IKEA PAX wardrobe systems?',
      answer: 'Yes. Multi-door PAX wardrobes and sliding mirror systems are notorious for bending if moved assembled. We dismantle the doors, shelving, drawers, and carcases systematically, transport them flat, and reassemble and level them perfectly in your new home.',
      display: true
    },
    {
      question: 'What happens to the small screws, wooden dowels, and shelf pegs during the move?',
      answer: 'We place all fixings into individual heavy-duty ziplock pouches clearly labelled with the specific furniture item and room name. These pouches are taped securely to the main frame so no crucial component ever goes missing.',
      display: true
    },
    {
      question: 'Do you carry your own tools, or do I need to provide screwdrivers and allen keys?',
      answer: 'Our crews arrive equipped with complete professional toolboxes, including powered torque drivers, hex keys, spanners, rubber mallets, and spare generic furniture dowels and furniture glides.',
      display: true
    },
    {
      question: 'Can you move heavy marble or solid hardwood dining tables in one piece?',
      answer: 'Solid marble and quartz tabletops must always be detached from their supporting plinths or trestle bases to prevent stress fractures across the stone. We crate or heavily blanket the stone slab and transport it on edge on our padded A-frame dolleys.',
      display: true
    }
  ]
};
---

<ServiceLayout service={serviceData}>
  <div class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none space-y-6">
    <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black text-navy dark:text-pearl tracking-tight">
      Stress-Free Furniture Disassembly & Reassembly Across London
    </h2>
    <p>
      Modern interior furnishings and historic period architecture are rarely in natural harmony when moving day arrives. Contemporary king-size ottoman beds, expansive L-shaped corner sofas, three-metre extending dining tables, and tall multi-bay wardrobes are simply too large to pass through the winding stairwells, tight ninety-degree landings, and narrow doorways typical of Victorian and Edwardian London properties.
    </p>
    <p>
      Forcing assembled furniture through constrained spaces results in gouged plasterwork, chipped door frames, and wrenched furniture joints. At <strong>Pearl Removals</strong>, our Cricklewood-based crews provide methodical furniture dismantling and reassembly as an integrated service, ensuring your furniture arrives and functions flawlessly in your new home.
    </p>

    <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-navy dark:text-pearl pt-4">
      Specialist Care for Engineered Flat-Pack & Modular Systems
    </h3>
    <p>
      Modern flat-pack furniture constructed from high-density chipboard and MDF requires delicate handling. Cam locks and wooden dowels easily tear out of their pilot holes if an assembled wardrobe is tilted or lifted by its top panel. Our team knows exactly where to deconstruct: removing hanging doors and internal drawers first to relieve frame tension before systematically unfastening the exterior carcase.
    </p>
    <p>
      We handle high-end European modular furniture—including bespoke Italian wardrobes, USM Haller modular steel systems, and designer shelving—with identical precision, using torque-limited drivers to prevent over-tightening or stripping delicate factory threads.
    </p>

    <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-navy dark:text-pearl pt-4">
      Antique Joinery & Heritage Timber Furniture
    </h3>
    <p>
      Antique wardrobes, four-poster beds, and Victorian extending mahogany tables demand an entirely different skill set. These pieces rely on traditional joinery techniques—such as hand-cut mortise-and-tenon joints, wooden tapered pins, and brass knock-down fittings.
    </p>
    <p>
      Our experienced movers never use brute force or power drivers on antique hardware. We carefully tap out wooden locking pegs, label left and right panels with non-residue conservator tape, and cushion every carved finial and pediment in thick cotton batting and transit blankets.
    </p>

    <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-navy dark:text-pearl pt-4">
      Plumbing, Levelling & Final Room Placement
    </h3>
    <p>
      London properties are famous for their character—and their unlevel floors. When rebuilding large wardrobes or shelving units on sloping timber floorboards in older properties, doors will stick or gaps will appear if the base is not properly shimmed.
    </p>
    <p>
      Our technicians use spirit levels and adjustable furniture glides or timber shims to square the foundation of every wardrobe before hanging doors. We fine-tune euro-hinges with multi-axis screwdriver adjustments so your wardrobe doors align with factory perfection before we pack up our tools.
    </p>
  </div>
</ServiceLayout>
